#passage(("Prophet Muhammadﷺ was a Bedouin Arab. He could not read or write, and he was among his people for 40 years before he received Revelation from God. His people knew him as The Honest, The Trustworthy. These were the titles that his people gave him, because it was a community-based life, so everyone knows everyone in the community. They used to entrust their goods with him and used to come back and everything was OK. They've never known him to lie.", "And they used to worship idols. Prophet Muhammadﷺ did not believe that what you make with your own hand is God. It does not make any sense to say: I made this with my own hand and this is God. You just made it with your own hand. Then Prophet Muhammadﷺ used to go to a cave called the Cave of Hira', and he used to reflect upon the Creation and try to worship God. And he had the first encounter with Angel Gabriel, in which the first few verses of the Quran was revealed. Then he went back to his wife, and then he was shocked, he was terrified, because he encountered something that was extraterrestrial, you can say. His wife [assured] him and she told him: You're good, so God will never do anything bad to you, because you're good to the people, you're honest, you do good things, you give charity, etc.", "And then Prophet Muhammad had other encounters and he had Revelation. The Quran was revealed in 23 years. Sometimes when Revelation came his wife was there, his companions were there; they saw the effects of Revelation on him. His wife, for example (the cold day in the desert is completely insane, because you got nothing to protect you from the cold), she said: He used to sweat in the coldest day from the Revelation coming on him. A human cannot replicate the idea of sweating in the coldest winter, but this used to happen because of Revelation. Another Companion: his leg (Prophet) was on the leg of the other Companion when Revelation came. He (Companion) said: I felt my leg was going to break from the weight of Revelation coming down. So these are certain incidents that happened while Revelation was coming down upon Prophet Muhammadﷺ.", "His mission was to call people to worship God alone, worship One Creator, not associate any partners with him (there's only one Deity worthy of worship), and to stop worshipping idols and things that you make with your own hand. And he was persecuted for 13 years because he was calling people to worship God alone. And those people were Bedouin Arabs that only believe in the religion of their forefathers, and believe that: You are disgracing us by saying, leave the religion of your forefathers. It was a cultural thing for them. Then he had to leave Mecca to go to Medina. And then they were also trying to attack him, until he took back Mecca from those Bedouin Arabs and they came back to their lands.", "And Prophet Muhammadﷺ continued to preach or tell people about God alone until he died, and then his Companions are doing the same: tell people about the Truth, because he came with the Quran, and the Quran is the Eternal Message until the end of time. It's for you and for me and for everyone, not for the Arabs, not for a specific group; it is for all the Creation, and it would remain until the Day of Judgement. So Quran is the Guidance for how to live your life, and to know right from wrong, to know what will happen in the Afterlife, to know the Attributes of God, to know some of the history of the past and the life of the Prophets; all of that is within the Quran.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Irrational Criteria For God's Existence! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xz7nptUD9Ug", ((1469, "24:29–24:52"), (1502, "25:02–25:34"), (1543, "25:43–26:29"), (1594, "26:34–27:05"), (1631, "27:11–27:38"),), id: 2194)
