#passage(("He says: Show me that Prophet Muhammad is an Ishmaelite, because you cannot inherit a covenant if you're not in the bloodline. What covenant are you talking about? That proves that this guy was never a Muslim, because we as Muslims don't believe that Prophet Muhammad inherits any covenants. That's a Christian belief. If you want to talk about that, it's even more a Jewish belief, not just Christian: this idea of the bloodline of David and being from the bloodline and inheriting covenants. We don't have that in Islam! It's not an Islamic belief. Allah chooses Prophets and Messengers not based on their race, but based on their piety and Allah seeing their hearts. So this claim itself is flawed, because we don't believe that Prophet Muhammad is a Prophet because he inherited his covenant based on his bloodline.", "But you said: show me that he was from the lineage of Ishmael. The funny thing that you do not know is that the Arabs have a tradition of preserving the lineages. So for example, Bukhari would report the lineage of Prophet Muhammadﷺ, and we have the full lineage of the Prophet Muhammad. We know that he was from Quraysh, and we know that the Arabs generally preserve their lineages. I'm going to tell you the lineage of Prophet Muhammad, from The Prophet all the way to Ishmael. The Prophet Muhammadﷺ, his name was Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah. The Prophet was Muhammad, the son of Abdullah, the son of Abdul Muttalib, the son of Hashim, the son of Abdul Manaf, the son of Qusai, the son of Kilab, the son of Murrah, the son of Kaab, the son of Luay, the son of Ghalib, the son of Fihr, the son of Malik, the son of anNadr, the son of Kinana, the son of Khuzayma, the son of Mudrikah, the son of Ilyas, the son of Mudar, the son of Nizar, the son of Ma'ad, the son of Adnan, the son of Ismael. So that is the full lineage of Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, from the Prophet Muhammadﷺ all the way to Ishmael.", "Now you do that with any Prophet or Messenger: you can't! Because other nations did not have this tradition of preserving the lineages, while the Arabs had. Your argument about the covenant is flawed anyway, but even so we're still giving you the lineage of Prophet Muhammad all the way from the Prophet himself to Ishmael. And secondly: nobody ever questioned that! Because the Arabs had a method of preserving their lineages, so they knew, each person, where did they come from. They were proud of their lineages, so they would preserve them. And until this day, many Arabs still keep that tradition.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| PBD Calls Me An Islamist?! Five Reasons To Debunk Islam?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S1CSlMRuy9s", ((1156, "19:16–19:52"), (1199, "19:59–21:07"), (1270, "21:10–21:48"),), id: 2196)
