#passage(("His people knew him as the Trustworthy, the Honest; those titles they gave him: الصادق الأمين. When they had disputes, they used to go back to him, because they trusted his judgment, and they knew he was not biased towards anyone; he's just sincere with everyone. His people used to worship idols. He believed that worshipping idols was not correct. Idols, you make them with your own hand; if you make them with your own hand, you can destroy them with your own hand. He used to move away from his people and go to a cave called Cave of Hira.", "What happened is he had an encounter with what we call Angel Gabriel. By the way, angels, we don't believe they're women with wings and this and that. We believe angels are creatures. We do not comprehend that as humans; they are in a completely different realm. He went back to his wife because he didn't know what happened to him, and he said: Cover me. His wife covered him. She said to him: You are good to everyone. You tie your ties of kinship; you feed the poor. Then he explained to her what happened.", "She took him to one of her cousins called Waraqa ibn Nawfal, who was a Christian person, a Christian in a sense. He used to read the biblical scriptures and things like that; he used to translate them. He told him that this was the same angel that came down on Moses, and he told him: You're a Messenger, an angel that comes to the Messengers. And your people will kick you out when you preach to them. I wish I was there to support you. So he said: Will they kick me out? As I just told you, they called him the Trustworthy, the Honest. Why would they kick him out? He was surprised. He said: Yes, they will kick you out, because every Messenger was kicked out by his people when he brought the idea of worshipping One God.", "So when he went and preached to his people, he said to them: If I told you there's an army behind this mountain, would you believe me? They said: Yes. He said: I'm the Messenger of God. They said: We don't believe you! Why? Because he said to leave the religion of their forefathers, and they wanted to follow the religion of their forefathers. So that's the start of Revelation in Islam. But the Quran came down through 23 years period; it didn't all come down in the cave of Hira like some people think. The first revelation was Surat Iqra', which happened in that cave.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslims Question Islam P1! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tjZje2tKQqQ", ((929, "15:29–15:55"), (966, "16:06–16:45"), (1008, "16:48–17:22"), (1047, "17:27–17:54"),), id: 2199)
