#passage(("This is another clear example of something ahistorical, 100%. First, the Constitution of Medina is not in The Quran. The Quran doesn't mention the Constitution of Medina at all, whatsoever. There's no such thing, and that's why he didn't bring a source for what he says. Then he says the Constitution of Medina included Zoroastrianism.", "The Constitution of Medina had different sections. It included believers and commandments to believers, and then even sections for the Jewish people. For example, Jewish people cannot go and fight outside the Medina without the permission of The Prophet, because it can influence the safety within the people of Medina. So the Constitution of Medina highlighted differences between the commands to believers and disbelievers, and what believers should do and what disbelievers are ought to do, and not ought to do, and the freedoms that they have. But it certainly did not include Zoroastrianism and everyone was one.", "That's not only ahistorical, but that's an outright lie about what The Quran teaches, because it's not in The Quran, and that's not what it says. That's why he didn't quote the Constitution of Medina. He just keeps mentioning it, but he never quotes it. He never says what it actually says.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Responding To Professor Jiang's Lecture On The Islamic Golden Age | Muhammed Ali!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SVGKQ-xiGs", ((2358, "39:18–39:33"), (2378, "39:38–40:01"), (2408, "40:08–40:22"),), id: 2205)
