#passage(("The people who persecuted him throughout all his life: how did he behave with them? How did he act to them? What did he do? How many years was he persecuted in [Mecca]? 13 years. So he was there for 13 years, and he's being persecuted. I want you to imagine this: him and his companions are being killed, [massacred], being killed. You hear the stories: they put him on the floor, in the heat of [Mecca]. This is boiling; if you put an egg, it will boil from the amount of the heat. In the midst of the sun, put a massive rock on, and he says: Allah is one, one. So he is affirming what he believes about Allah. The reason he says that is because the [polytheists] of Mecca believed in Allah, but they were associating, worshiping other gods, intermediaries. So what he's emphasizing there is just one: there's only one, and I will stick on my belief that there is just one.", "So you see all this persecution, you see the killing of the companions of the Prophet, you see the persecution to the prophet himself: he's praying, and they put their leg on his neck while he's prostrating on the floor, almost suffocating him, and then [Abu Bakr as-Siddiq] comes and he pushes [them] away and say: Do you kill a person just because he says my Lord is Allah? Muslims were peaceful; they were not trying to do anything to you. Prophet, he says to the people: Worship [one] God alone, do not worship idols. So for 13 years this is happening.", "I want you to imagine now the amount of pain: 13 years. Some of us, our family members or our coworkers, just one situation is enough for you. Your own brother, blood brother, one situation: Close the door, I'm not going to talk to him again. Your family members, your colleagues, your friends, whatever it is, you close the door. Prophet sallallahu alaihi [wasallam]: for 13 years attempts of murder, killing actual people of the family member, etc.", "And when the conquest of [Mecca] happens, and they surround the Pagan Arabs with a massive Army, then the Pagan Arabs surrender; they're outnumbered. And then the prophet sallallahu alaih wasallam slaughters everyone? Is that what happened? No. But shouldn't we expect that to happen? If that happened, isn't that justified? 13 years of persecution, killing and murdering him and his companions, and now you are in a position of power, now you got authority and power. Expected and justifiable and understandable for you to take revenge, vengeance. No one is going to blame you for 13 years being persecuted. But the prophet, he let them go free, and we need to understand this. Some of the companions are not okay, not happy with this: These are the people; they were murdering us, they killing us, they were doing everything to us. But this is the mercy [to] mankind, Prophet Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wasallam.", "And from that we learn that this is how we should be as well. We take the prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam as our example. It's not about our emotions. Emotions, it misguided many people, just as it does with many of the Christians — you just tell them stories — or does with many of the misguided groups. Emotions is always used as a tactic. We have to be, as Muslims, sticking to the Quran and Sunnah in our dealings and our behavior and our teachings before we focus on anything.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((1137, "18:57–20:37"), (1237, "20:37–21:21"), (1281, "21:21–21:53"), (1313, "21:53–23:01"), (1381, "23:01–23:35"),), id: 2209)

