#passage(("The topic of discussion is what occurred between the Christians of [Najran] and the prophet, peace be upon him. The caller, who refers to himself as Nightmare, says that there was a debate between the two parties. CP, on the other hand — Christian Prince — holds the view that there was no debate, but the prophet, peace be upon him, completely avoided it.", "There's nothing in the text that says that they never met him. The text clearly says that they argued or debated about Jesus. This is the first lie. The second lie is that he says that this means that [yujadilunahu] means they spoke against him, and this is false; it refers to a discussion.", "Third lie: CP uses the term [yujadilunahu fihi] to express that the prophet, peace be upon him, wasn't present. Now this is false again. [Fihi] means about him: that they were arguing with the prophet, peace be upon him, about him, him being Jesus.", "There are two possible scenarios. The first is that Christians argued with the prophet, peace be upon him, while they were in [Najran], which was three weeks away from Medina. Now, unless they took the 7:30 flight, I don't see how they could have made it on time, tomorrow, as the report says. The other scenario is that they were already in Medina and had a discussion, as the report plainly says; then they were invited to invoke the curse of Allah on the next day.",), "Farid Responds, “Christian Prince Hangs Up (BUSTED!) [Lies #54-56]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NiKl7kVFIco", ((10, "0:10–0:30"), (134, "2:14–2:47"), (209, "3:29–3:44"), (224, "3:44–4:16"),), id: 2210)

