#passage(("24/7 Christians have nothing to say, except this. There's nothing about Islam. They wake up in the morning: 'Aisha! They sleep in the night: 'Aisha! Their alarm: A'isha! 'Aisha! That's how their life is.", "The funniest thing I'm going to tell you about these Christians specifically is they have, in their own tradition, rabbis admitting to this, that Isaac married Rebekah at the age of three. If you make the calculation, it had to be the age of three. So you see the age of Sarah, the age of Abraham, all of that. It had to be from 3 to 10. That was her age. So they have that in their tradition, the church fathers explicitly making statements about the age of marriage. They have no age of marriage in the Bible, actually, at all. Zero, there is no specific description, but they just come and try to make these absurd comments. All it talks about in the Bible is puberty. If you read Ezekiel (16:7-8) — I'm not going to get into the verses, because they're very graphic — where it talks about the woman is ready. It talks about her physical... going through puberty. It talks about her body parts, which we're not going to talk about. This is what the Bible talks about when it comes to when is the woman ready for marriage or intercourse or whatever term you want to use. And they still try and make these arguments. I don't know how!", "And the most important thing is this: if one Muslim comes and says, I believe that 'Aisha (May Allah be pleased with her) was 25 when the Prophet married her — hypothetically speaking, which is not the case — if he says that, is there any issue with him being a Muslim? Is he not a Muslim now? No! There's no issues at all. Why? It's not one of our Articles of Faith! We don't say \"believing in Allah, the Books, the Messengers, 'Aisha's age!\" These are not the articles of faith that Muslims have. So this criticism that they have, it's not a criticism against the religion, because someone can still hold the belief, because just the age of one of the wives of the Prophets when he married her, that information is not relevant to the foundations of the faith. None of it is going to refute the religion if you say she's that age or that age. But this is the only thing you can hold on to — clutch to straws — because they have no substance when it comes to arguing actual foundations, like the reliability of their scriptures, evidences for their beliefs that they have, their creeds. This is what we argue when it comes to arguments from a Muslim perspective. This is not even an important matter to discuss. Red herring, like some people would say.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Canadian Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XhEel3w9jYY", ((1957, "32:37–32:50"), (1975, "32:55–34:00"), (2046, "34:06–35:39"),), id: 2215)
