#passage(("As simple as that. It doesn't come down to arguments like that; it comes down to the positive arguments for Islam. And if the positive arguments for Islam are solid enough, and they are, then this is irrelevant; bringing this up is not even worth looking at. The problem would be with those that have an issue with it, and that's David himself admitting it.", "Now, why this is so interesting, especially to me, is because this is David's third main argument against Islam: a video made with Sam, and they go through the top 10 arguments against the prophet, and this is number three. What's so ironic about this is that Sam and David and Anthony, they want to end [Uthman's] career, flew all the way to San Diego, and this is what they have: they just gave up on the third strongest argument against Islam. I agree with what David's saying; it makes perfect sense to me. Is this growth by David? Because the previous video was several years ago. Maybe he's grown; maybe he's realized that it's not really that strong of an argument. Maybe he realized this on the spot, when Uthman came to him with this argument that God cannot be in the womb of a woman; maybe it's at that point that he realized that even the age of Aisha thing is irrelevant to the whole discussion.",), "Farid Responds, “David Wood Gives Up on Age of Aisha Argument!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hXXoVeM650o", ((177, "2:57–3:29"), (214, "3:34–5:29"),), id: 2216)
