#passage(("Under 18 is a new modern definition of a child. A child in the dictionary was always, until late 1900s, someone who didn't reach the age of puberty. Open any dictionary. When the Prophet ﷺ was with Aisha, at six years old that was a contract. There was no physical interaction between him and her. So when she reached the age of 9, she herself said that a girl becomes a woman when she reaches the age of 9.", "The Bible doesn't have an age of marriage. What does the Bible say about the age of marriage? You can marry a one year old according to the Bible. It doesn't say you can't, which means it's not wrong, because there's nothing that prohibits you from doing it. Aisha was not a child, she was a woman. She reached the age of puberty, she menstruated. And menstruation is the last period of puberty.", "There is something called نكاح (Nikah), which is a marriage contract. So that marriage contract is a promise that that person you are married to, no one else can marry them, but that does not allow you to have intercourse or engage with that person in a sexual way. So I can do that with babies. People do that even today, they still marry babies. They say, my baby is for your baby; they're going to get married when they are old. That doesn't mean now the babies are doing things with each other. This is a perverted mentality to have, honestly. We don't look at things this way.", "We see the Prophet ﷺ, from our perspective, was the best human being walking on Earth at that time. So Abu Bakr, which was his closest companion, which cares about his daughter more than anyone would ever care because it's his own daughter, he made that [contract] with Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, because he wants to secure the best man out there that exists. If you saw a man that you know his character was the best, you know his money was the best, you know that was the best person around, you would try to secure him for your daughter if you could.", "So you wouldn't know more than the mother and father of Aisha, and you wouldn't know more than her, that she lived 50 years after the Prophet. She was the happiest woman; she praised the Prophet ﷺ for 50 years after him. She had all the right to say whatever she wanted, if there was any abuse or anything. She was teaching Muslims; she was one of the biggest Scholars. The companions used to come ask her questions, because she lived with Prophet Muhammad ﷺ; she described his life. She said, for example, Prophet Muhammad never put his hand on a woman ever in his life; that was how she described it. She said he was the most controlling person of his desires.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts His Best To Disprove Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zGjHDTtZLko", ((132, "2:12–2:47"), (224, "3:44–4:21"), (283, "4:43–5:06"), (310, "5:10–5:32"), (334, "5:34–6:06"),), id: 2221)
