#passage(("In America, it was seven years old in Delaware. It was 10 years old in other states. And these were Christian countries. They were following the Bible a lot more than they do today. They were ruling by Christian rule. But they knew according to the Bible it's puberty, and girls reach puberty at these ages. So it's okay for you to get married so long as you're being good to the girl. It's marriage, it's not fornication. You're getting married, you're staying with that person, taking care of them. That was allowed.", "Now, is that it? No. In America today, the age of marriage in four of the states is zero. There is no age of marriage. You can get married at any age today, with the judge and parent consent, like in California and four other states. It's not just America. Many other countries, with the judge and parent consent, they make exceptions: if the parents agree and the judge agrees and sees the case she's ready, they agree. There was boys married at age of 10 and girls as well, in the US, in the last 15 years or 10 years. So, you want to come and talk about Prophet Muhammad? You're going to have to condemn entire human history and your book first, which talks about 8 years old puberty.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Hate Preacher Attempts To Disrupt Civil Muslim-Christian Dialogue! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X05zRHM4kVs", ((1806, "30:06–30:34"), (1836, "30:36–31:45"),), id: 2224)
