#passage(("Now, I'm going to mention just a few things from history. You have a professor, for example, Professor Margaret Wade. She has a book about medieval times. She said: it needs to be remembered that many medieval widows were not old. They were often married between the age of five and 10, might find themselves widowed in their teens. It's a professor telling you, not Muslim telling you that. You have a Professor Richard Worthley and Professor Stephen. They say: in medieval and early modern European societies, age of marriage remained low. We're documenting cases of brides as young as 7 years, although marriage was not typically consummated until the age of puberty. You have the chief judge Richard A. Posner. He says the law governing the age of consent has changed dramatically in the United States. During the 19th century, the age of consent was 10 years old. I can present more and more references.", "You'll get someone who says, \"I condemn all of these people. I condemn all human history.\" So, why am I mentioning these things? Because as a Muslim, if you're educated, if you understand this was known and being practiced in the entire history of humanity, why am I feeling ashamed? It's liberalism and modernism and feminism and this idea. There's nothing for you to be ashamed of. If you know the history, you would mention the history to the people.", "You'll get some people who will tell you, \"That was in the past. I condemn it. We don't have this happening today anymore.\" Independent has an article: over 200,000 young marriages. Where? In the US. And this, by the way, doesn't include some of the states that don't have a minimum age, like California. It reaches 200,000 cases in the last 10 to 15 years, I believe. And it mentions a girl: she was 14 and she got married to someone who was 74 or 76 or 70 something. I'm not talking now about 200 years ago. I'm talking about today.", "Today they have a difference between age of marriage and age of consent. Over 30 states of America allow marriage of people who are under age, or, let's use the word, minor, under their normal age, 18, with a parent and judge consent. So, this is today. If anybody comes to you in the West and they have an issue with this, tell them: go fix up your countries. Deal first with your PDF leaders, mentions in the files, that you are happy sitting down not complaining about, and go deal with these marriages first. When you deal with your own marriages in your own society happening today as we speak, then come and talk about our prophet.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Was Aisha 18 Years Old When She Married The Prophet? | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5lzZclwwqDg", ((513, "8:33–10:16"), (616, "10:16–10:41"), (644, "10:44–11:15"), (675, "11:15–12:26"),), id: 2226)
