#passage(("One of his wives was Safiyya bint Huyayy. Huyayy ibn Akhtab, her father, was the leader of the Jewish tribe Banu An-Nadir; he was the leader of one of the main Jewish tribes. His daughter, she got married at 10, not to the Prophet, to someone else. This was the custom, this was the culture, this was how things were happening. Even if you go back 1400 years ago, it was less life expectancy, we had less advancements.", "So, just looking at it from that perspective, all of those people who come with these things are just uneducated. What we do is respond by educating them on these issues by saying: you have an issue, so you have to bring the rational justification to show me why this is a problem. You’re making the claim, not me; you’re saying X is immoral. I don't need to provide anything, to justify anything. That’s my belief, and that’s historically accurate. But you just didn’t do your research. If you’re making a claim that there’s a problem, then come and justify it. Tell me why there’s an issue in this.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Questioned About The Prophet's Marriage! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lzXN6Mv9k8A", ((596, "9:56–11:02"), (667, "11:07–11:34"),), id: 2227)
