#passage(("You don't see Muslims going around today getting married at this age, whether it's at 9 or 12. You don't see that happening, because Islam doesn't prescribe that to us. Marriage is one of the things that we call from the customs. So the customs of the time, this was the common thing. People died very young as well. You didn't have the medicine we have. So people had to multiply. They fought in wars.", "So today, that's an exception, and scholars put extra conditions, like father's agreement, so they make sure that this is governed, done in the right way. If there's any harm, then say no: not allowed to do this. So Islam is very detailed. You don't just say do this or don't do that. No, there's laws for every single thing.", "You have to go back: where is the source of morality? Here is the source of morality in Islam, and here's the reasoning. I'm giving you the wisdoms and reasoning behind the source of morality, cuz it's objective. It's from God. Now if someone is not religious, you can say it's my opinion based on my culture, and I'll tell you the same thing: cultures differ. If morality is relative, then there's no morality, just depending what the society thinks in that day.", "If someone says I'm Christian, I say okay, Christianity: the Bible, Ezekiel, talks about the girls being in the marriageable age; it talks about her body parts growing, which is puberty essentially. You have, for example, the biggest church fathers being [betrothed] or getting married at the age of 12 or whatever. The age of marriage was even 12 of the church and the Roman Empire at the time. This was how things were.", "So Muslims today live their lives, no problem. You get married like everyone else gets married, and if there is an exceptional case, okay, present: why is this a good thing? For what reason? What is the benefit for the child? I haven't seen anything like this in my life, cuz today it doesn't happen, because the cultural norms change, and marriage is a cultural practice. So you can change with the norms. And Allah tells us in the Quran: if the culture is something, command to do that thing, as long as it doesn't disagree with God or is very bad. Then you can follow that, like how you dress or how you do certain cultural things.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Shocked By Muslim After Questioning The Prophet's Marriage! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SxG2d79W6j0", ((1591, "26:31–27:06"), (1662, "27:42–28:14"), (1696, "28:16–28:38"), (1718, "28:38–29:10"), (1756, "29:16–29:54"),), id: 2228)

