#passage(("What age is the right age? What age does a person become an adult? What's the right age where someone becomes ready for marriage or adult or whatever? But that's a circular argument: you're saying an adult is who you say is an adult.", "Some countries will say, okay, age of consent is 16; some others will say it's 18; some countries will say 14. Philippines, I believe, not too long ago, or Japan had it 12; they changed it recently as well. Countries keep changing. Question is: what's the age? Someone says the age is 16. Okay, so if you are 15 years old, 364 days, 23 hours and 1 minute less from the next day, you're not an adult, but a minute later you magically become an adult. How does that make any common sense? So in Islam, that's not how we view adulthood.", "Now, why am I taking you to history? Cuz a lot of people today look at a [9-year-old] of today or 7-year-old of today, 6-year-old of today, and they impose that six-year-old in the past. Things were very different. Why? There was no elementary school, kindergarten, high school. The kid will be born, the daughter will be there, her next step in life is to get married. This is how women were functioning in society. Traditional kind of household: guy goes to work; the woman, she helps in the household. When she becomes adult enough, then she gets married and she has children. Today it's a complete different story, and things are designed in a complete different way.", "So we cannot look at a 9-year-old of today, who doesn't deal with adults because we keep them with children like themselves. They don't mature quickly. At that time, even when you were younger, you would already be dealing with adults; [you'd] be going to trade with your mother and father. So their maturity psychologically was different. Once you reach puberty, then you're no longer a child. Then marriage is based on the parents. They look at you and they say: okay, ready for marriage? Not ready for marriage? That's what your mother and father would decide, looking at you.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Shocked By Muslim After Questioning The Prophet's Marriage! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SxG2d79W6j0", ((202, "3:22–3:44"), (271, "4:31–5:04"), (307, "5:07–5:46"), (346, "5:46–6:30"),), id: 2229)
