#passage(("I'm not saying it was right \"because of the circumstances\"; I'm saying that this is God's command. All the Prophets of God have done it, and these women were OK with it, because this is a Prophet of God! Which woman wouldn't want to be with a Prophet of God? Who is going to treat you better? None of these women complained about this reality. So I'm trying to say it was agreement, this took place, there was no issues.", "Do you know when a woman's brain is fully developed scientifically? It's 25 years old. And that's why the brain full development is not a criteria for marriage, or else you'll put the age of marriage as 25, which is ridiculous, because you don't need a full developed brain to get married. That's not criteria that anyone makes. So that's the first thing.", "The second thing, about the physical part: what science says about the physical development. Once a woman goes through puberty, is she now a woman who's able to get married and give birth? Biologically, she can have children. If she goes through puberty, by definition, she can have children. I'm not saying this is right, but I believe the youngest woman in history was four or five that gave birth. But that's an extreme example that is bad; we're not agreeing with that. But that happened in human history, actually, but that's an exceptional case.", "What ages do women go through puberty? From what age to what age? There is, I believe, a book (I'm forgetting the author: Robert Kail & John Cavanaugh), it's called \"Human Development\", that shows, even historically, the case wasn't 12 to 14. So what we have today is not different from how it was in the past. So today is from 8 all the way to 14 or 15, and 14-15, that's late puberty, by the way. And 8 is early, but it's within that range. And that's why the age of marriage in the UK in the 1800s was seven years old; in the US, it was 10, and seven in Delaware, according to William Blackstone in his book \"Commentaries on the British law of England\". That was 200 years ago, let alone many years in the past.", "So a woman can go through puberty; if she does, then you cannot argue physically anymore that the woman is not physically mature. And, I told you, psychologically you cannot make the argument of a full brain, or a complete brain development. They cannot argue that.", "People keep bringing this argument, and we find it ridiculous, because the overwhelming majority of Muslims are marrying very late, today and in the past. We don't have people going in lines doing this. The issue is not going on. That's what I'm refuting. You read propaganda online; it doesn't mean it's true! In reality, go watch the stats of Muslim countries, the average age of Muslims get married. The stats are there, no matter what these people bring: one exceptional case of one crazy person. There were so many photos that are lies, and circulated, and people who are not critical thinkers fall for things like this. They circulate pictures of a guy with his granddaughter, and they claim that this man is marrying his daughter in Pakistan or whatever. Sickening people, liars.", "So in reality, there's nothing in Islam that teaches you to marry a girl that is young. In Islam, there's a criteria. The criteria is the physical and mental maturity. It's a very simple thing: if there is any harm on the girl, it is Haram (prohibited) for you to consummate the marriage. If there is a harm that is established, you're not allowed to do it. If the girl is not ready, and it's going to cause her psychological harm, you're not allowed to get married! There's no age in Islam. There's no specific age. There is the person individually; you have to look at them, and whether they're ready or they're not ready.", "And women in the deserts, actually, grow quicker physically than they do in the cold. They conducted studies, many studies on fish: they applied heat, and in a hot climate, you grow faster; in cold climates, you grow slower but more. So the point I'm trying to make is, nobody has any arguments here to present, scientific or otherwise.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Wife Grills A Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tUX4xfgST_E", ((1304, "21:44–22:02"), (1423, "23:43–24:15"), (1457, "24:17–25:04"), (1535, "25:35–26:20"), (1585, "26:25–26:34"), (1604, "26:44–27:58"), (1689, "28:09–28:44"), (1726, "28:46–29:02"),), id: 2230)
