#passage(("The last claim he makes: he quotes the verse of the Quran where it says \"Hatta idhā balaghū an-nikāḥ\", when they reach a marriageable age, or nikāḥ. That's what the verse says: when they reach nikāḥ, if then you sense from them maturity. But what is this nikāḥ that they reach? Go to the mufassirūn, the exegesis. It's not something which is disagreed upon. Go to the classical scholars. They will tell you here is referring to puberty: when they reach puberty. Nikāḥ is puberty, age of puberty. And Aisha herself reported that a girl becomes a woman at the age of nine. And Aisha reached puberty that time. So this verse actually is going to be evidence against you.", "And it doesn't matter if the Ottoman Empire had the age 15. I didn't even confirm this. Even if this is true, it doesn't change anything. The Ottoman Empire towards the end: there was a lot of secularization taking place and all of changes happening towards the fall of the Ottoman Empire. It doesn't prove anything. And if we take that claim about 15 years old, that goes against you actually, because you're saying 18, and that doesn't work even if we said it's 15.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Was Aisha 18 Years Old When She Married The Prophet? | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5lzZclwwqDg", ((3158, "52:38–53:24"), (3205, "53:25–53:47"),), id: 2231)
