#passage(("Words in language have definitions. So not your definition, but the linguistic definition of the word \"child\". What is a child? Who hasn't hit puberty, we can say, simply. By the way, in all dictionaries (until some dictionaries only recently changed a little bit here and there), open any dictionary in human history, a \"child\" was someone who was under the age of puberty. Now, did 'Aisha hit the age of puberty before the consummation in the marriage with Prophet Muhammad? She did, so why use the term \"child\"? Why are you using a dishonest term? Under an objective factor reality, she wasn't a child with the definition of \"child\".", "Prophet Muhammad made a contract with her 3 years before consummation, and she wasn't with the Prophet in the house. So a marriage contract does not mean intercourse. It does not mean physical engagement with the person in Islam. You can have a marriage contract as assurity that you are with this person, but it does not necessitate any physical contact. So 'Aisha was still with her family after that marriage contract was done, until she reached puberty, and then the consummation took place.", "So why would the Prophet wait, if it was about young girls and all of this nonsense that people say? Why would he possibly wait until she hits the age of puberty? Because by definition, the people who do these things, when you use the term \"children\": once you hit puberty, you're expired for these people. It just makes no sense! Why would you wait until that happens? That is the exact opposite of what you would want if you were that type of person.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Confronts Muslim On The Marriage Of The Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vz1jgBpf8UE", ((1028, "17:08–18:01"), (1088, "18:08–18:43"), (1126, "18:46–19:08"),), id: 2233)

