#passage(("Regardless of what position you take on Jesus, I'm going to use the Bible. Where does the Bible tell you what is the correct age of marriage? There isn't. So if God didn't tell you which age it is, then where do you get that moral teaching? Of course, there are Christians who would refer to verses in Ezekiel, for example, the book of Ezekiel, which talks about puberty (Ezekiel16:4-8). So it talks about the woman's development of puberty, and they would reference that as the thing that we can use to give us an indication that a woman is ready. But there is nothing in the Bible, the whole Bible, from beginning to end, whether it is Old or New Testament, that talks about the age of marriage.", "Morality comes from God. Morality comes from the Creator only. Human beings cannot make moral judgments; it would be subjective, and therefore it's not binding. So if morality comes from God, and God doesn't tell you what the age is, then under what basis are you criticising Prophet Muhammad for marrying any age? What is the moral criteria that you're using to say that this was something that is not \"great\", or \"this is wrong\", or whatever term you want to use?", "Your subjective opinion, it's not a criteria for morality. Where do you bring that it is morally wrong? Not societal opinions, not emotional views, not \"I think this\", \"but it looks like that\", \"but it feels like this\". It's irrelevant; that's not where we get right and wrong from. It's not feelings. Your feelings are not the arbiter for us, and we are not going to be judged by the opinion of you. We're not going to take you as the moral standard of a whole 2 billion people who are Muslims.", "So you're using a subjective view of a person who's born somewhere in Europe in the 21st century. What they taught you today is what you're using as a criteria to determine that this is correct or incorrect. And that is subjective. You are a product of your own society, and your society is not like every other society; therefore it is not a criteria, due to the fact it's being subjective, to make moral judgments over other societies.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Confronts Muslim On The Marriage Of The Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vz1jgBpf8UE", ((251, "4:11–4:59"), (301, "5:01–5:31"), (361, "6:01–6:33"), (423, "7:03–7:24"),), id: 2237)
