#passage(("Aisha’s age and her marriage has nothing to do with Ali ibn Abi Talib. Ali ibn Abi Talib was the cousin of the Prophet ﷺ; he’s got nothing to do with Aisha رضي الله عنها. He’s got nothing to do with her age, and if any issues happened, they happened later on, way later on after the death of the Prophet ﷺ, years and years, tens of years later, anything that happened between her and Ali رضي الله عنه.", "We’ve got Aisha herself telling us her age when she got married. We've got multiple reports from her, and then we’ve got multiple reports from different individual people. She said that in the most authentic books of Hadith. She said her age, she said the age where the marriage contract happened, then she said the age where the consummation happened, as well. She was very specific about the age. There’re many people in the community; this was a well known thing.", "The people who try to change the age, why do they do that? Because they fall on the bandwagon of being on the defensive for no reason. They’ve already lost the battle, because they’re defending something that they’re not supposed to defend, because the person who’s making the attack is the person who needs to justify. But what happened is they think that they need to justify something. They don’t have pride and honour in the tradition. They don’t understand history and what actually happened in history. And, based on that, they’re trying to change the teachings of Islam, those types of people writing those articles. So, if she says her age, who knows her age more than her?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Questioned About The Prophet's Marriage! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lzXN6Mv9k8A", ((790, "13:10–13:27"), (812, "13:32–14:11"), (855, "14:15–14:46"),), id: 2242)
