#passage(("Prophet Muhammad had two kind of stages in his mission of giving the Message: one was in Mecca, and one was in Madina. The initial stage of Mecca, of calling people to God, was 13 years. In Mecca, Prophet Muhammad started calling people to God, he barely had any followers, or weak people; people were accepting Islam gradually. That was the initial stage of calling people to God. The Quran was revealed in 23 years. A portion of the Quran was revealed in Mecca, and Prophet Muhammad was prohibited from fighting anyone in his Meccan period.", "Towards the end of the 13 years, because people were accepting Islam, the disbelievers of Mecca plotted to kill the Prophetﷺ, so he had to migrate and leave, or he was going to be killed. The Prophetﷺ left Mecca and went to Madinah. When the Prophetﷺ went to Madinah, the disbelievers of Quraysh didn't stop there. The people in Madinah, all of them (there was two tribes, Aws and Khazraj), they welcomed the Prophet and they accepted Islam. No war, nothing, by choice! They believed in the Message of Prophet Muhammad, they were waiting for him, and when he came, they accepted his Message.", "Now, the disbelievers of Quraysh knew that this man has the Truth. And people are accepting the Truth. And if we don't kill him, the whole Arabian Peninsula is going to become Muslim, and that's what happened in the end. They knew that this was going to happen, so they wanted to end his life! So the first thing that happened was the battle of Badr. The disbelievers of Quraysh with a 1000 army and weapons attacked the Muslims in Madinah. It was a DEFENSIVE battle. They were 300, outnumbered three to one, and they fought back against them and they defeated them.", "Throughout the 13 years, they were plotting to kill him. His uncle was protecting him, which is the only reason, you can say, that this attack did not go so far.", "These people keep attacking the Prophet, but now it's a counterattack. The Prophetﷺ took an army of 10,000 people and went for the conquest of Mecca. If we were to apply this logic that people bring with attacking the Prophet, then the natural thing will be he'll take back his revenge! The Prophetﷺ said to them, you are free, أنتمُ الطُّلَقاء. And he let them go. And he said, there is no blame on you today. Imagine 13 years! Us as human beings, someone does something bad to you once, you spend your entire life not talking to them. 13 years of persecution, the Prophet comes back and he let them go free, when he's in a position of POWER! And that's what MERCY is.", "Because people talk to us about Jesus being merciful, but Jesus was never in a position of power! And you can't compare Jesus to Prophet Muhammad when he was never in power. Jesus spent 3 years of ministry. He was in a position of weakness under Caesar, and he said to the people, (give to Caesar what is due to Caesar), (Mark12:17): pay him taxes. So you cannot compare 23 years of a life of a person, 13 years in persecution, then he had power, to someone who never had power. That's not a fair comparison.", "Mercy is given when you are in a position of power. Yes, Jesus said to the people, \"Oh, forgive\", but he was not in a position of power. So that's not the real definition of mercy, because you're not in power anyways. What can you say other than that? Even if you don't say, \"Let them go\", you cannot say: go attack them, because you're weak! So, it's not really mercy to say to the people, \"Be merciful!\", when you're weak. Mercy is when you're in a position of power and authority, and you still choose to forgive people. So, this is the life of Prophet Muhammad.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Wife Grills A Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tUX4xfgST_E", ((156, "2:36–3:10"), (197, "3:17–3:53"), (236, "3:56–4:26"), (293, "4:53–4:55"), (313, "5:13–6:34"), (398, "6:38–7:10"), (432, "7:12–7:37"),), id: 2281)
