#passage(("Now, the Prophet tried to go to certain places in order for him to invite them to Islam. He went to اَلطَّائِف‎ (atTaif) first. When he went to atTaif, he was hit with stones. He bled until his feet stuck to his sandals! They didn't accept his Message; he had to come back. And then, we believed that the angel came to The Prophetﷺ and he told him, shall I close the two mountains on them? And the Prophet told him: no, that maybe from their ancestors, there will come people who will do Tawheed (Monotheism), only worshipping Allahﷻ.", "Prophet Muhammad then went to Madinah, which is Yathrib (because it was called Yathrib at the time), and the people there accepted him and welcomed him. Then the Prophet in Yathrib, what did he do? He prepares an army and go attack Makkah? No! He did have an army, of course. The people of Yathrib believed in him. Other people believed in him around Yathrib as well. So the people in Makkah were not happy, because they were accepting the Message of this man. This man is going to remove the worship of idols that we have, so they prepared the army, and they went to attack the Prophet. The Prophet defended himself.", "The Prophet, before his death, was preparing an army to go and fight the Roman Empire. Do you know why? The Romans were already attacking the Muslims!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “2 Jews Question The Truth of Islam! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kKviK80NYiM", ((917, "15:17–15:49"), (957, "15:57–16:37"), (1050, "17:30–18:15"),), id: 2283)
