#passage(("Says that in around 627 AD the prophet of Islam raided the Jewish tribe [Banu Qurayza], killed all the males who had puberty [hair]; on that day he killed more than 600 [Jews]; then he took their sons as working slaves, but took the girls and the women as sex slaves to be divided among his men. Multiple things here need to be not just put into context but corrected. However, I focused on the main thing, which is this huge part of context, the historical context that he's leaving out, which is [Banu Qurayza] had double crossed their Muslim allies during the siege of Medina and had chosen to ally with their enemies [that] were going to annihilate them. Let's not forget that minor detail.", "This is what he says next: \"Didn't break any treaty. [When] the battle of the trench happened, Muhammad sent for help. They didn't want to help, because they were supposed to be neutral. Muhammad got mad at them; that's why he raided them right after the battle of the trench.\" So now he's arguing that they're neutral. That's the main point here: they didn't betray Muhammad, they were neutral. Now, I've read the classical sources, I know what's in there, so naturally I ask him to establish what he's saying using his source.", "So he says, read the biography of [Ibn Hisham]. This is what [Ibn Hisham] has to say: \"On the night of the Sabbath of [Shawwal], fifth after Hijra, it came about by God's action on behalf of his apostle that Abu Sufyan and the chiefs sent some of their number, saying that they had no permanent camp, that the horses and camels were dying; therefore they must make ready for battle and make an end of Muhammad once and for all.\" Why are they talking to [Banu Qurayza] about this? What are they expecting? Are they asking permission from [Banu Qurayza]: can we raid the Muslims? Is that what's going on?", "They replied that it was the [Sabbath]. Sabbath is going to prevent them from what? Well, clearly they're neutral, so it's going to prevent them from providing an answer? \"They reply that it was a Sabbath, a day on which they did nothing, and it was well known what had happened to those of their people who had violated the Sabbath. Moreover, we will not fight Muhammad along with you until you give us hostages.\" They want hostages, and if they receive hostages they will fight Muhammad. \"Until you give us hostages whom we can hold as security until we make an end of Muhammad, for we fear that if the battle goes against you and you suffer heavily, you will withdraw at once to your country and leave us, while the man is in our country and we cannot face him alone.\"",), "Farid Responds, “How Bad is Brother Rasheed? (Top Christian Apologist in Arabic)”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QUEdjFWRaSA", ((71, "1:11–1:56"), (168, "2:48–3:39"), (276, "4:36–5:36"), (341, "5:41–6:50"),), id: 2289)
