#passage(("If we return to the actual hadith that's being quoted, we'll find that it actually falls a bit short. The report in Arabic speaks of what we refer to as [Abhar], which should not be confused with Elwatin or the aorta. By returning to the works of classical linguists and classical scholars, we find them clearly differentiating between [Abhar] and Watin; we find several scholars specifically stating that Abhar is located in the back. This has been made clear by linguists such as Erami Eliari and others. Now, Dr. David Wood would have realized this if he knew some Arabic.", "However, there's another point that needs to be highlighted. As David rightly states, these verses were revealed in Mecca, which means that Allahh allowed the prophet to get away with reciting the Quran and attributing things to him for over 10 years. Let's go back and check out the verses in the full context: \"And if he, i.e. Muhammad, had made up about us some false sayings, we would have seized him by the right hand. Then we would have cut from him the aorta. And there is none of you who would prevent us from him.\" The verses suggest immediate action. Now nobody could have prevented Allah subhana tala from taking away the life of the prophet peace be upon him. Well, except according to David Wood's understanding: the only thing that could have prevented Allah is the spectacular immune system that the prophet peace be upon him had, which allowed him to survive the poison for around 4 years.", "Now David himself quotes a narration that states that [Bishr], the prophet's companion, also ate from the same food and died on the spot. The same narration states that a dog also ate from the food and also died on the spot. I add that the prophet peace be upon him continued to spread Islam during those four years, conquered Mecca, spread Islam through Arabia, and only at the final pilgrimage he recited these words. Allahh says, \"Today I have completed your religion for you and I have perfected my favor on you and I'm satisfied with Islam as a religion for you.\" The [deen] was complete. If Allahh wanted the prophet peace be upon him dead for lying, then that would have happened way before the completion of the religion. The fact that the prophet peace be upon him was able to survive poison that powerful, and the fact that he was able to complete his mission just 3 months before dying, well, that kind of sounds like divine intervention to me. In fact, the prophet peace be upon him was only sick during the last 10 days of his life. This suggests that the effects of the poison were held back for all that time.",), "Farid Responds, “The Prophet's ﷺ Aorta / Poison Argument [Response to David Wood]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OrRGXi8-Pyc", ((62, "1:02–1:45"), (108, "1:48–2:50"), (170, "2:50–4:08"),), id: 2297)
