#passage(("Allah says in the Quran (alHaqqa69:44-47): لَأَخَذۡنَا مِنۡهُ بِٱلۡیَمِینِ (We will seize him by his right hand), meaning we will take his life. And the لام (Lam) there in the Arabic language, لَأَخَذْنَا, that means we'll do it instantly. So if he lies, if he just thinks about lying, we'll instantly take his life. ثُمَّ لَقَطَعۡنَا مِنۡهُ ٱلۡوَتِینَ: then, ثُمَّ (thumma) here is for something that happens 'after' something else.", "That's very important here, because the verse is giving us an order of two things: first, God will take his life, then God will cut his aorta; not God will cut his aorta, then take his life. The verse says ثُمَّ, which is for order here, that one thing will happen after another. And it's called الترتيب مع التراخى: that something will happen after a while from another thing. So, what will happen instantly? That God will take his life. The second thing that will happen, God will cut his وتين (wateen). The word used in the Quran is وتـيـن.", "Now, what is the story that these Christian apologists and liars bring up? After Prophet Muhammadﷺ completed the entire mission of giving his Message, and the last verse of the Quran was revealed (alMaida5:3), and the Prophetﷺ told the Muslims that he's going to die, that God revealed to him that he's going to die, after all of this happened, when the Prophetﷺ was dying in his last sickness, he said he feels some of the poison that he was poisoned by a Jewish woman. And then he says, \"I feel AS IF\". What does \"as if\" mean? It feels like something's happening to him. So then he said, as if my أبهَر (abhar) are being separate. He doesn't say it is being separate, he says as if is being separate.", "Then the Prophet refers to that poison. That poison happened to the Prophetﷺ in the year of خيبر (Khaybar), 7AH, 3 to 4 years before the death of the Prophet. There was a Jewish woman that said, I'm going to poison this man, and if he's a true Messenger of God, he wouldn't die. So she came and she brought food with poison. His companion ate and he died instantly, because it's poison! Then the meat itself informed the Prophetﷺ, which was a miracle, that the meat is poisoned. Then the Prophetﷺ asked her why she did that. Then she admitted; she said that she was testing the Prophetﷺ, if he was a Messenger of God. So he's referring to that poison, because the Prophet ate from it first, but he didn't die like the Companion that died. So that's another miracle. So you have two miracles there in that report alone.", "All you need to do is just to read the argument itself, to read the verses of the Quran, to read the actual events, and you realise how these two things have no relation to one another. It doesn't matter even if it's the same word. Let's assume it was Wateen in both of them. It's not Wateen, but let's assume it's Wateen: how does the argument hold? Argument doesn't hold still. It doesn't matter, because the Prophet completed his Message. This was not that, after he lied, God took his life, and then severed his aorta. That didn't happen. Whichever way you want to look at it, there is no argument there.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Prove Christianity After Questioning A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ev6mWbHq80U", ((1815, "30:15–30:42"), (1847, "30:47–31:15"), (1888, "31:28–32:45"), (1969, "32:49–33:44"), (2055, "34:15–35:11"),), id: 2298)
