#passage(("Allah told the Prophet Muhammed that the meat was poisoned. So, he was informed in that narration. So, if we were to accept that this incident is true, we have to also accept the information in the incident: that there's divine revelation given to this Prophet that this meat is poisonous, or we reject the whole tradition. So, either we accept this narration or reject the narration, one of the two things; you cannot pick and choose. You leave the miraculous part of the narration, where God has told him that this has Poison, and you accept the part where he was poisoned.", "So, we're saying the Prophet was poisoned at that time. Allah says in the Quran (alMaida5:67), very clearly, that Allahﷻ is going to protect the Prophet. Allah says (O Prophet deliver that which was given to you from your lord), and وَاللَّهُ يَعْصِمُكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ (Allah will protect you from the people). Meaning: Allah will protect you until you FULLY deliver the Message. So, Prophet Muhammad is a human being; his protection extends to the delivery of the Message.", "Allah revealed in chapter:5 of the Quran, in the beginning, the first few verses, Allah said: (Today I've perfected your religion, and completed my favour upon you) (alMaida5:3). Many of the exegesis believe this was the last verse that was revealed in the Quran.", "The Prophet became sick towards the end of his life, and in his illness he said to 'Aisha that he feels pain from the poison that he ate. Now the Prophet didn't say I'm dying because of the poison, because that's an instant poison: the Prophet would have died straight away. If he was lying about God, God has taken his soul from the beginning. He wouldn't have reached that point where everything is delivered, and then he tells the people: This is the last sermon that I'm going to be given. And he gives the last sermon, and then he dies after!", "The word used in the Hadith is not the same word used in the Quran, about the Aorta; it's a different word, and it can mean something else. He said: انْقِطَاعَ أَبْهَرِي, which can mean vein, can mean multiple things, and the Aorta specifically is used الْوَتِينَ in the Quran. So, the reason he didn't die, and it was three years, is because Allah promised to protect him until he finishes his delivery of the Message.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Questions Muslim On The Death Of The Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QJpQp5i26Vc", ((190, "3:10–3:36"), (216, "3:36–4:00"), (275, "4:35–4:49"), (304, "5:04–5:40"), (353, "5:53–6:38"),), id: 2299)
