#passage(("Some Christians are saying, and making a comment saying: But he died. If you want to talk about a human being, Prophet Muhammad in the end was a Prophet; all the Prophets died. If you look at the belief: Moses died, Solomon died, David. All of them died; every Prophet will die!", "I'm responding to the argument \"but he still died\". If you believe Jesus was God, God in your belief died! So if dying was an issue, how did The Creator of the whole universe, The God of everything, die, in your belief? And you have an issue with a human being, Prophet Muhammed, dying? That makes Zero sense for anyone!", "Prophets die, and Jesus will die. We believe he will die too. If Allah delayed his time for a bit, that means he has a mission, but then he will die just like anyone else will die. So, every human being will die, and that's what the Quran says (alImran3:185): (Every soul shall taste death) كُلُّ نَفْسٍ ذَائِقَةُ الْمَوْتِ; nobody escapes death. Allah says directly to the Prophet Muhammad (azZumar39:30–31): إِنَّكَ مَيِّتٌ وَإِنَّهُم مَّيِّتُونَ (You're going to die and they're going to die), and then you will all be resurrected. This is being said to the Prophet before his death. We know that Prophet Muhammed is going to die. Allah says in the Quran (alImran3:144) that (If the Prophet died, then you will turn on your back?) You can not turn on your back now. The Prophet is a Messenger, he is giving you a Message; you're supposed to worship God. He's here for an appointed time to fulfil a duty and then he's going to go, just like Jesus was here for an appointed time and he left.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Questions Muslim On The Death Of The Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QJpQp5i26Vc", ((495, "8:15–8:27"), (524, "8:44–9:02"), (562, "9:22–10:15"),), id: 2302)
