#passage(("I'm joined, alhamdulillah, by Dr Mohammed Abdul Rahman, who's a neurologist with a sub-specialty in epilepsy and EEG. Today we're going to be talking about the question of: was Rasulullah a victim of epilepsy?", "This is a video response to some research that a friend of the channels has been working on for a very long time, I think maybe a year or two, and this is his baby. He spent a lot of time on this; he took university courses on this, I believe courses had to do with neuroscience, and he's been boasting about his research for a very long time. And when I saw the video, I honestly was surprised. I do believe that a lot of what he brought forward can be responded to from a hadith lens; however, it's great to have a professional on board, a neurologist who knows the subject and knows the intricacies of the symptoms and diagnosing these matters.", "Was he born premature? I'm not aware of anything like that. He had many revelations throughout a period of 23 years: hundreds, maybe thousands.",), "Farid Responds, “Neurologist debunks ex-Muslim! [Epilepsy Argument Deflated]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sejJCQYAvaI", ((4, "0:04–0:25"), (44, "0:44–1:40"), (356, "5:56–8:07"),), id: 2309)
