#passage(("I'd like to point out something in regards to the lack of documentation of a seizure. Non-Muslim audience members, and perhaps even some Muslims, would maybe assume that, hey, the Muslims themselves chose not to document this: seizures occurred, but they didn't document this. I say that this is impossible, because the early Muslims, the Sahaba, the [Tabi'in], the early historians documented everything. Remember, these are the same people that brought to you the satanic verses; these are the same people that brought you information about Rasulullah marrying Zainab; these are the same people that brought you every single argument that Islamophobes use and critics of Islam use against the prophet peace be upon him. So it's extremely, extremely unlikely that a hundred thousand companions would simply ignore seizures occurring. That's just from a historical point of view.", "The Quran itself often quotes and preserves the arguments that are brought forth by non-Muslims. So they accused him of being a poet or a sorcerer or someone who is insane; however, they never accused him of having seizures. So that's another point.", "I would like to briefly elaborate that all the reports that speak of the prophet peace be upon him contemplating suicide are disconnected, and therefore we do not accept these as authentic.",), "Farid Responds, “Neurologist debunks ex-Muslim! [Epilepsy Argument Deflated]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sejJCQYAvaI", ((1083, "18:03–19:18"), (1172, "19:32–19:55"), (1367, "22:47–23:01"),), id: 2310)
