#passage(("When he speaks about the ringing of the bells, he mentions something really interesting towards the end. He says it comes in the form of the ring of the bells, and also comes in the form of a man who speaks to him. So I find this really interesting, because this implies that this is something that people saw. This shows that the Quran isn't from rasulullah himself, because there's someone who's actually teaching him the Quran. Now it's not something that can be shrugged off as a hallucination; it can't be shrugged off as some sort of symptom for some sort of neurological disease. It's a man who comes up to him, who teaches him the revelation, and it's a very eye-opening report, because it's something you just can't shrug off.",), "Farid Responds, “Neurologist debunks ex-Muslim! [Epilepsy Argument Deflated]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sejJCQYAvaI", ((1465, "24:25–25:21"),), id: 2316)
