#passage(("The part about the hadith of the bees and the sounds of the bees: well, it seems like Dr. [Jalaluddeen] isn't quite sure how to interpret that, and he's provided multiple explanations for that hadith. By the way, if I was him, if I was in his position, I'd actually say: Hey, I don't accept this hadith. It sounds like a supernatural event. It's something that conflicts with reality, so I'm just going to reject it. But do you know why he insists that this is evidence for a seizure or epilepsy? It's because he's invested too much time into this. He's put in over four years into building these arguments, and he just doesn't want to take the L.",), "Farid Responds, “The Most Desperate ex-Muslim”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vuN8BwMnzL8", ((369, "6:09–8:04"),), id: 2317)
