#passage(("The hadith says that he moved his lips; it doesn't say smack his lips. That's the first thing. It says he's moving his lips, he's moving his tongue in order to keep up with the revelation. It doesn't even say that in English: in English it says \"moving my lips\", it says the prophet used to move his lips. The word smacking isn't even in English.", "So a verse is actually revealed that tells him to stop moving his tongue in such a manner, and after that he completely stops moving his tongue and mouth in such a manner. Report says that he sticks his head down when the verses are revealed to him, and then he just recites them from memory after that.",), "Farid Responds, “Neurologist debunks ex-Muslim! [Epilepsy Argument Deflated]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sejJCQYAvaI", ((1702, "28:22–29:43"), (1809, "30:09–30:36"),), id: 2318)
