#passage(("Now let's check out how this was dealt by Dr [Jalaluddeen]. Hey, why don't you play the rest of the clip? You know which part I'm talking about. Now do you know why he paused at that specific point? Well, it's because he assumes, and by the way he's right, he knows that you're not going to return to the original video, because, hey, let's face it, most of us are just too lazy. And again, yes, he'd be right, because most of us are quite lazy; we're not gonna bother to return to the original clip. Unfortunately for him, I'm not most people, and it was a direct refutation to me, and now thousands of people are aware that he wasn't able to deal with my argument.",), "Farid Responds, “Refutations 101 [Crash Course]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CgfiwsD4Sns", ((2143, "35:43–37:40"),), id: 2319)
