#passage(("Multiple people could see the angel when he came in the form of a man, so there are no hallucinations that are happening there. It's quite clear if you go through the biography of the prophet peace be upon him: you'll notice that the prophet is clearly receiving orders from another man. You can't shrug this off as a hallucination. Rasulullah interprets this as an angel in the form of a man. Yes, you can shrug that off; you can say: no, it's just a man. You can do that, but why would it be a hallucination? Why would that be a hallucination if multiple people see a man?", "There's a very quick point in regards to this hadith of [Jibril] shifting positions: the report is disconnected; it's not authentic.",), "Farid Responds, “Ex-Muslim Refutes Himself!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TKEODlSjdX0", ((89, "1:29–2:15"), (286, "4:46–5:00"),), id: 2325)
