#passage(("If you thought that the claim that rasulullah had epilepsy was a desperate one, then wait until you check this out. You see, genetics play a role in epilepsy, and for Dr [Jalaluddeen] to make the case that rasulullah had epilepsy, he wanted to argue that he has a family history of it. So he claims that rasulullah mother had visual hallucinations, and that means that she may have had epilepsy.", "So the response to this is very simple: this isn't even a real hadith. You can't find it in any classical sources, but Dr [Jalaluddeen] doesn't really seem to care. He found this in a blog, a blog that of course doesn't even cite the reference for this report. Now you shouldn't really be surprised, because this is the level of doctor [Jalaluddeen]. Unfortunately, his trusty sidekick shamil doesn't really know any better.", "Now this is how desperate these [mortals] are: they find a report that says that the prophet's mother had a dream, and they're like, oh, dream means vision, and therefore she had visual hallucinations, and if she had visual hallucinations, then she probably had epilepsy. Now you see, there's nothing here that even says that there was a vision or hallucination or anything like that. All of the report says is that it was said to her. So maybe Dr [Jalaluddeen] can argue that since we don't know who's saying [this], perhaps it may have been an auditory hallucination. That's the most that can be said.", "But more importantly, let's go back to the origin of this report. Ibn [Kathir] here is quoting [Ibn Ishaq], and [Ibn Ishaq] doesn't mention his source for the report. There is no chain. If we return to ibn [Hisham], this is what we find, and of course ibn hisham is quoting [Ibn Ishaq]. So [Ibn Ishaq's] source is this. Now this is not a reliable source of information. No, you weren't able to establish a single hallucination, let alone three. The most that you were able to do is argue that she had a single dream.",), "Farid Responds, “Now they say his MOTHER ﷺ had Epilepsy!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-RjGA0XyGwA", ((1, "0:01–0:31"), (103, "1:43–2:09"), (164, "2:44–3:35"), (215, "3:35–4:52"),), id: 2330)

